@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ The following options are provided to configure the output:
 * **`SEPARATOR`**:
     The text string used to set the footnote separator. Defaults to `:`.
 
+* **`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`**:
+    Whether to number and order footnotes by the order in which they are
+    defined (`True`) rather than the order in which they are first referenced
+    in the document (`False`). Defaults to `False`.
+
+    By default, footnotes referenced in the body of the document are numbered
+    in the order in which they are first referenced. Footnotes which are only
+    referenced from within other footnotes follow, and any footnotes which are
+    never referenced are listed last, in the order in which they are defined.
+
